                        "tags": [
                            "future"
                        ],
                        "form": "буду/будешь… изгаля́ться"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b4929802-10d8-3b8d-8e27-5b8d07231b87",
                        "entry_id": "05139776-d4c2-375d-bcb0-5a107ac13874",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. зло насмехаться; издеваться, глумиться"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "abc68caf-7a89-42b3-88f5-f94c9171f5b3",
                                "sense_id": "b4929802-10d8-3b8d-8e27-5b8d07231b87",
                                "text": "— Да ведь я-то гладка, а он, пёс, того глаже… Изгалялся всяко, плетьми стегал."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "70988fa4-dec3-4ba7-977b-45646bc0ece5",
                                "sense_id": "b4929802-10d8-3b8d-8e27-5b8d07231b87",
                                "text": "— И не ори, а то хуже будет. — Над старухой так изгаляться!.. — Ты всю жизнь над людьми изгалялась ― и молодая и старая."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f5be221-28a0-4dba-8a51-7404476c77ce",
                                "sense_id": "b4929802-10d8-3b8d-8e27-5b8d07231b87",
                                "text": "Мне б огреть тебя плетьми, // Четырьмя али пятьми, // Чтобы ты не изгалялся // Над сурьёзными людьми!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f87c372-c148-4d0b-9b69-f9b9859ae326",
                                "sense_id": "b4929802-10d8-3b8d-8e27-5b8d07231b87",
                                "text": "Он ждал, что над бумагой снова, как бывало прежде, начнут изгаляться, обхохатывать её, но нет: в воздухе вокруг словно бы разлилось почтение, бумагу бережно свернули, вернули ему, после чего он был спрошен, уже без прежней развязной хамовитости, а уважительно, и одним, а не всеми разом."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3b16c1f7-3301-485f-8e0a-2a75b6c48c1e",
                        "source_entry_id": "05139776-d4c2-375d-bcb0-5a107ac13874",
                        "source_sense_id": "b4929802-10d8-3b8d-8e27-5b8d07231b87",
                        "target_lang_word": "jeer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jeer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "84e23316-eb45-3721-b417-fd0fd27ce0d6",
                                        "entry_id": "c9345463-ff41-34f3-b737-bde512bec60b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mocking remark or reflection."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "462181dd-f268-4926-9408-d6761f4d2961",
                                                "sense_id": "84e23316-eb45-3721-b417-fd0fd27ce0d6",
                                                "text": "1711, Jonathan Swift, The Fable of Midas, in The Works of Jonathan Swift, D.D., Vol XII, Sir Walter Scott, ed., Edinburgh: Archibald Constable and Co., 1824, pages 302-5,\nMidas, exposed to all their jeers, Had lost his art, and kept his ears."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "jeer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bca2c8bc-4ad9-3b1c-9ce9-c437e01f48a5",
                                        "entry_id": "3fea69e9-cc3e-3ac1-ad4a-3627276c2f67",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To utter sarcastic or mocking comments; to speak with mockery or derision; to use taunting language."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a36a31ad-64fb-4b27-ae41-07670f22881b",
                                                "sense_id": "bca2c8bc-4ad9-3b1c-9ce9-c437e01f48a5",
                                                "text": "But when he saw her toy, and gibe, and geare, / And passe the bonds of modest merimake, / Her dalliance he despisd, and follies did forsake."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87522bf7-f706-4b4b-bb31-33bb0700ea2a",
                                                "sense_id": "bca2c8bc-4ad9-3b1c-9ce9-c437e01f48a5",
                                                "text": "At the end of a frantic first 45 minutes, there was still time for Charlie Adam to strike the bar from 20 yards before referee Atkinson departed to a deafening chorus of jeering from Everton's fans."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a990884f-adb9-36ab-af12-7cb9c5b9fbc8",
                                        "entry_id": "3fea69e9-cc3e-3ac1-ad4a-3627276c2f67",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To mock; treat with mockery; to taunt."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c969a90-6c5e-4c07-a01d-cf5290bcfabe",
                                                "sense_id": "a990884f-adb9-36ab-af12-7cb9c5b9fbc8",
                                                "text": "And if we cannot jeer them, we jeer ourselves."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "jeer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aec28ccd-d46c-38d0-bc1a-0a8afcb71b5d",
                                        "entry_id": "b51ba9e2-5f1d-37d3-91ff-ac5509e78a7b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A gear; a tackle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b3f156c-b877-36b2-8ad6-fb41aff35426",
                                        "entry_id": "b51ba9e2-5f1d-37d3-91ff-ac5509e78a7b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An assemblage or combination of tackles, for hoisting or lowering the yards of a ship."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in-plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da6e61a8-727e-4acb-8dfd-6b9f3ef8d7db",
                                                "sense_id": "6b3f156c-b877-36b2-8ad6-fb41aff35426",
                                                "text": "In the nineteenth century, 1811 to be exact, the jeers were unrove after the yard was slung, the weight of the yard being borne by chain slings. The jeers used then were a treble block lashed to the mast head through a hole in the center of the top"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dfe4f912-2f2d-49a4-8a16-ef36a6e411ad",
                        "source_entry_id": "05139776-d4c2-375d-bcb0-5a107ac13874",
                        "source_sense_id": "b4929802-10d8-3b8d-8e27-5b8d07231b87",
                        "target_lang_word": "mock",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mock",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3edfd2cd-3b74-3437-9916-8ec808b13cb8",
                                        "entry_id": "58d874f2-c767-32f2-a2d4-b746cd50341a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An imitation, usually of lesser quality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe9f3db8-7689-425d-8b40-cf1778f5add0",
                                                "sense_id": "3edfd2cd-3b74-3437-9916-8ec808b13cb8",
                                                "text": "Is tortured thirst itself too sweet a cup?\nGall, and more bitter mocks, shall make it up."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fb4e070f-d072-3ce6-b37a-74a64c631fe2",
                                        "entry_id": "58d874f2-c767-32f2-a2d4-b746cd50341a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mockery; the act of mocking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bc437d0-889c-4322-86df-6b14aa57fdd5",
                                                "sense_id": "fb4e070f-d072-3ce6-b37a-74a64c631fe2",
                                                "text": "Fooles make a mocke at ſinne: but among the righteous there is fauour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2641a090-fa22-495a-baa1-28412c718bae",
                                                "sense_id": "fb4e070f-d072-3ce6-b37a-74a64c631fe2",
                                                "text": "Thus says my king; an if your father's highness\nDo not, in grant of all demands at large,\nSweeten the bitter mock you sent his majesty,\nHe'll call you to so hot an answer of it"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14b2a19d-b3fb-3668-abbc-148e53da1eda",
                                        "entry_id": "58d874f2-c767-32f2-a2d4-b746cd50341a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of mock examination."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7e77ea1-404a-4563-9347-55a9c6217523",
                                                "sense_id": "14b2a19d-b3fb-3668-abbc-148e53da1eda",
                                                "text": "He got a B in his History mock, but improved to an A in the exam."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14470945-4b2e-3f5f-9295-348fc58334c9",
                                        "entry_id": "58d874f2-c767-32f2-a2d4-b746cd50341a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mockup or prototype; particularly, ellipsis of mock object, as used in unit testing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ba9afc5-fd35-47e3-b91d-e9fa4f60f0f8",
                                                "sense_id": "14470945-4b2e-3f5f-9295-348fc58334c9",
                                                "text": "You can, if you must, create a mock that derives from a concrete class. The problem is that the resulting class represents a mix of production and mocked behavior, a beast referred to as a partial mock."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47435f44-157f-45f2-9a28-9c9b3dd4a47a",
                                                "sense_id": "14470945-4b2e-3f5f-9295-348fc58334c9",
                                                "text": "Mocks replace the objects with which your methods under test collaborate, thus offering a layer of isolation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mock",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60a29039-29fc-392e-8a5b-c38141ea3413",
                                        "entry_id": "9c431144-9cfb-38fa-b5ce-3ce52c9bf355",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To mimic, to simulate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5cd32216-0070-4405-be6c-d889a2c0ff5c",
                                                "sense_id": "60a29039-29fc-392e-8a5b-c38141ea3413",
                                                "text": "To see the life as lively mocked as ever / Still sleep mocked death."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "901bc6a5-7520-4dfe-84ef-39c358bf4d8d",
                                                "sense_id": "60a29039-29fc-392e-8a5b-c38141ea3413",
                                                "text": "Mocking marriage with a dame of France."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f7d90d1-12dc-3fd9-a2ba-cbb872cdde61",
                                        "entry_id": "9c431144-9cfb-38fa-b5ce-3ce52c9bf355",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To create an artistic representation of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c55d6d5-5a4e-4f4e-86f4-e3d8085392b4",
                                                "sense_id": "9f7d90d1-12dc-3fd9-a2ba-cbb872cdde61",
                                                "text": "[I]ts sculptor well those passions read / Which yet survive, stamped on these lifeless things, / The hand that mocked them and the heart that fed: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b65535c-0cd2-35dc-8570-3b166e682027",
                                        "entry_id": "9c431144-9cfb-38fa-b5ce-3ce52c9bf355",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make fun of, especially by mimicking; to taunt."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a63a9a15-e4bd-42bf-a050-d91a8eeae3c7",
                                                "sense_id": "2b65535c-0cd2-35dc-8570-3b166e682027",
                                                "text": "And it came to paſſe at noone, that Eliiah mocked them, and ſaide, Crie aloud: for he is a god, either he is talking, or he is purſuing, or hee is in a iourney, or peraduenture he ſleepeth, and muſt be awaked."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4744a648-d96b-4185-9811-b8663a70e00e",
                                                "sense_id": "2b65535c-0cd2-35dc-8570-3b166e682027",
                                                "text": "Let not ambition mock their useful toil."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ec6c98b-7161-3995-8800-9cc451d399d6",
                                        "entry_id": "9c431144-9cfb-38fa-b5ce-3ce52c9bf355",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To tantalise, and disappoint the hopes of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a38a04c-2414-4a2c-b8cb-0f28037b8dda",
                                                "sense_id": "3ec6c98b-7161-3995-8800-9cc451d399d6",
                                                "text": "The wind is mocking my efforts to light a fire!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd720a08-0ce8-4473-9125-daa857966a50",
                                                "sense_id": "3ec6c98b-7161-3995-8800-9cc451d399d6",
                                                "text": "\"It is the greene-ey'd Monster, which doth mocke / The meate it feeds on.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4659fa30-a081-402f-a9fd-d139ca3da23e",
                                                "sense_id": "3ec6c98b-7161-3995-8800-9cc451d399d6",
                                                "text": "And Delilah ſaid vnto Samſon, hitherto thou haſt mocked me, and told me lies: tell me wherewith thou mighteſt be bound."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64d2f9ad-f8ac-4f3a-a94e-a2d56e1bc741",
                                                "sense_id": "3ec6c98b-7161-3995-8800-9cc451d399d6",
                                                "text": "Why do I overlive? / Why am I mocked with death, and lengthened out / to deathless pain?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "abeb0525-3d65-4a67-9680-5f7c3e6bf54b",
                                                "sense_id": "3ec6c98b-7161-3995-8800-9cc451d399d6",
                                                "text": "He will not […] / Mock us with his blest sight, then snatch him hence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a904c27-c00a-40d5-9dc1-7ea9a1a0c764",
                                                "sense_id": "3ec6c98b-7161-3995-8800-9cc451d399d6",
                                                "text": "‘Mock’ certainly never signifies to loath. Its common signification is, to disappoint."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ea8fa2e-5ded-4dac-ac7e-c6cc410a5b21",
                                                "sense_id": "3ec6c98b-7161-3995-8800-9cc451d399d6",
                                                "text": "The French revolution indeed is a prodigy which has mocked the expectations both of its friends and its foes. It has cruelly disappointed the fondest hopes of the first, nor has it observed that course which the last thought that it would have pursued."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7639d3e0-5e70-325e-a206-78cd214bef91",
                                        "entry_id": "9c431144-9cfb-38fa-b5ce-3ce52c9bf355",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To create a mockup or prototype of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b2ff4dc-17c3-4cbb-b5fc-275dfd9f1c81",
                                                "sense_id": "7639d3e0-5e70-325e-a206-78cd214bef91",
                                                "text": "They can also mock other integration points such as backend, database, or any other external resource."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
